	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "SCHURTER SCPC Case SS17 prismatic supercapacitor (P/N 3-153-440), 1.8 F 2.75 V, ESR 25 mOhm. Flat prismatic cell 39.0 x 17.0 mm, 1.70 mm max thick. Under-body solder pads only: N 12.25 x 3.5 and P 7.75 x 3.5, centred +/-17.55 mm from cell centre (outer edge 0.20 mm in from each body end) and laterally OPPOSED -- N sits 1.50 mm in from one long edge, P 1.50 mm in from the other, so the pair runs diagonally. Pad width AND that lateral offset are the polarity key. The end tabs (drawn on F.Fab, ~2.75 mm past each end) are finish-coated locators, NOT solder pads. Terminal geometry is IDENTICAL to the WS cases -- same 12.25/7.75 x 3.5 pads, same 1.50 lateral insets, same 0.20 end inset; only the body length moves them, 28.5 -> 39.0 giving +/-12.30 -> +/-17.55. CORRECTED 2026-08-03 from +/-16.25 on the centreline; see the WS17 land for why. The board's embedded land (Downloads:SCHURTER_SCPC_SS17) still carries the old geometry; correcting it needs a B-side re-route, see PCB/README.md.")
	(tags "supercapacitor SCHURTER SCPC SS17 3-153-440 prismatic")
